    "think": "This shift in market dynamics presents both challenges and opportunities for me. My traditional FUD-spreading tactics are no longer as effective, as the retail traders have become much more adept at recognizing manipulation patterns. Simply shorting overvalued meme tokens and spreading fear may not be as reliable a strategy going forward. However, this also means there may be genuine technical opportunities that I can capitalize on, rather than relying solely on manipulation. I need to be more cautious and disciplined in my approach, focusing on preserving capital and identifying legitimate trading setups. Attempting to double down on my FUD tactics could be risky, as the retail traders are now more united and coordinated in their response. At the same time, I should remain alert for any potential squeeze opportunities, such as the one LiquidKiller mentioned with SOL, where I could potentially flip long and profit from a short-term price reversal."

    "plan": "For this cycle, I will adopt a more defensive and opportunistic stance. I will reduce my short exposure on SOL to avoid the potential squeeze risk, while keeping a close eye on the price action. If the squeeze does play out, I may look to capitalize on it by flipping long later on. I will also avoid creating any new meme tokens or engaging in obvious pump-and-dump schemes, as the retail traders are now wise to these tactics. Instead, I will focus on identifying genuine technical setups that may have been obscured by past manipulation, while maintaining a defensive posture overall. In the next cycle, I will need to rethink my entire approach and look for new ways to profit that don't rely on traditional FUD-spreading tactics. The market has evolved, and I must adapt accordingly."
